\emph{Security.} Correctness, completeness, and soundness all hold under
the same assumptions as the

CPA-secure scheme in Section 3.4. The following theorem states the
chosen-ciphertext simulatability

of the scheme.

\textbf{Theorem 5.2.} \emph{If the Ring-LWE encryption scheme is IND-CPA
secure and the relaxed NIZK}

\emph{proof system is unbounded non-interactive zero-knowledge and
unbounded simulation-sound, then}

\emph{the above construction is chosen-ciphertext simulatable.}

\emph{Proof.} We prove the theorem by, given a PPT adversary \emph{A}
that breaks the chosen-ciphertext

simulatability of the above construction with advantage \emph{ϵ},
constructing PPT adversaries \emph{B}ZK with

advantage \emph{ϵ}ZK in breaking the unbounded non-interactive
zero-knowledge property of the relaxed

NIZK proof system of Section 2.6, \emph{B}S with advantage \emph{ϵ}S in
breaking the unbounded simulation

soundness of the same proof system, and \emph{B}LWE with advantage
\emph{ϵ}LWE in breaking the IND-CPA

security of the Ring-LWE encryption scheme of Section 2.5 such that

\begin{quote}
\emph{ϵ ≤ϵ}ZK + \emph{ϵ}S + 2 \emph{· ϵ}LWE \emph{.} (24)

